+# Current-source Mac composed lifecycle check
+
+The optimized executable from committed source `6330b2d42050b46c2019e558074e087ed281e56a`
+completed 1,000 fresh composed windows and the exact version-2 plan of 33,000
+acknowledged native/owner actions. The unchanged strict validator returns
+`PASS_SCOPED_NATIVE_CASE`. The controller exited zero after 11,530.226 seconds
+(about 3 hours 12 minutes), with no stop reason, error or cleanup error. Its
+recorded group absence and a later independent process-table query both found
+the exact owned PID/group 28898 absent. No other owned native or heavy build/test
+job ran during this campaign; this does not establish continuous global host
+isolation.
+
+## What this covers
+
+Each fresh window requires the current text/editor history, virtual grid and
+outline completion, tree accessibility disclosure, modal open/close, color
+controls, ListBox accepted/rejected/repeated selection proposals, named
+Canvas2D selection and breadcrumb paths. Every cycle publishes the fixture's
+1,000 fully contained dense-label predicates, with 15 exposed tree rows, before
+teardown. ListBox checks require ordinary native host/row identities, accepted values
+and clipping. Tree/canvas checks additionally require current generation and
+scope against owner publication by the bound fixture. These are native API and toolkit
+routing observations. Requested 1920×1080 logical geometry and toolkit clipping
+do not establish physical display size, occlusion, pixels or physical pointer
+behavior. Earlier 24/26-step results do not substitute for this 33-step mix.
+
+There are 33,054 queue attempts and admissions for 33,000 completed actions.
+Fifty-four action records retry once, across 52 cycles: tabs 31, component-list
+21, disclosure 2. Queue admissions are not accepted callback counts. Retry causes
+were not observed, so no cause is assigned to the parent-graph optimization,
+native input ordering, machine load or another actor. Action elapsed guards
+include fixture settling/completion work and are not UI-frame or physical
+input-to-present latency measurements.
+
+The final main-thread snapshot records zero outstanding tracked native
+operations, accessibility windows, file panels and pending callbacks; menu/tray
+targets are retired. It also records one hidden, inactive, untitled Cocoa window
+at `[0,446,54,54]`, and `Menu.OriginalRestored=false`. This does not qualify zero
+Cocoa windows or original-menu restoration. The process subsequently exits and
+fresh process/group absence is checked; the pre-exit hidden window is not claimed
+to survive process exit. The fixture requests no general clipboard or OS preference changes and
+explicitly disables window geometry persistence. Its reported false clipboard/
+preference flags do not independently observe global OS state.
+
+## Sampled memory and retained evidence
+
+Forty-one forced-GC samples cover cycle 0 and every 25 completed cycles. Across
+all samples, live Go heap ranges from 30,153,056 to 50,844,552 bytes and RSS from
+184,909,824 to 403,210,240 bytes; goroutines range from 6 to 8 and end at 7. From
+cycle 25 onward, Go heap ranges from 44,365,752 to 50,844,552 bytes and RSS from
+373,866,496 to 403,210,240 bytes. RSS increases from 374,259,712 bytes at cycle 25
+to 403,210,240 at cycle 1,000. These observations do not prove leak-free or
+unbounded-retention behavior. Historical window-ID tombstones are retained.
+The 512 MiB Go-heap/1 GiB RSS limits are safety guards. This composed interaction
+fixture is not the empty 1,000-control baseline and does not qualify its
+40 MiB/150 MiB budgets or attribute native/GPU/private bytes. The final Go heap
+profile is 485,651 bytes; it is not a native/GPU allocation profile.
+
+The native invocation uses `-composed -cycles=1000 -sample-every=25 -timeout=4h`
+and the bounded heap-profile option, under the existing shared native lease and
+human-return markers. The source-bound build records 4,490 tracked and 6,229
+prepared dependency files, actual build metadata and an executable SHA-256.
+Source, binary, pinned harness and raw-log stability are checked through cleanup.
+The full stdout is 14,125,140 bytes with SHA-256
+`53631800025ebfa04f14c64e82c3296379eecd3e5b73fcf2b07ced0be4ecdcb6`;
+stderr is empty. The strict validator runs once after actual terminal evidence,
+with exact event/action order, completions, geometry predicates, samples,
+bindings, scope flags and cleanup checks. Internal review reports no unresolved
+findings. The earlier controller-fault and failed-soak records remain preserved.
+
+The raw trace/profile, receipts, producers, fixture context, source/build maps,
+predecessor scheduling-failure evidence and internal review are indexed in
+`records/archive-index.json` and retained in `records/evidence.tar.xz`. Private
+executables are excluded and identified separately by receipts. Saved producers
+retain original absolute paths; this is an evidence bundle, not a portable
+replay or executable distribution. `records/qualification.json` binds the exact
+scoped checkpoint and archive. No diagnostic draft added after source `6330b2d`
+is qualified by this run.
+
+## Remaining Mac work
+
+This completes the current-source 33-step lifecycle execution gate only. The
+original eight-hour soak remains failed (`soak occluded state drift`); a successful
+overnight and full app-wide idle wake/present evidence remain required. The
+ordinary 4 ms p95/6 ms p99 frame targets are still failed. Native/GPU memory,
+physical pointer and display scaling, human IME/VoiceOver, interoperability,
+distribution and full P4/P6/P9/P11/Mac acceptance remain open. Parent-graph
+validation is outside exact TotalUIWork timing; this lifecycle run is not a
+whole-frame performance comparison or proof of an ordinary latency gain.
